  published jar does not carry. Nothing in it is compiled or patched.

raylib examples
---------------
  Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Ramon Santamaria (@raysan5) and contributors
  Licensed under the zlib/libpng license.

  The demos (<demo>/src/net/b12n/raylib_jnk/scenes/) are ports of raylib's
  own example programs to jank. They are altered versions: the logic is
  reimplemented in jank, and the interop constraints described in
  raylib-jnk's guide forced structural changes throughout. Every demo's
  docstring names the upstream C source it was ported from (e.g.
  core/core_basic_window, shapes/shapes_bouncing_ball), and its
  docs/guide/index.md repeats it in a "Ported from" line.

  One deliberate behavioural deviation from the originals, applied uniformly:
  every example sets FLAG_WINDOW_HIGHDPI.

